            "xml": "<ns0:comment xmlns:ns0=\"https://uniprot.org/uniprot\" type=\"induction\">\n        <ns0:text evidence=\"8\">Part of the probable 17 gene mamAB operon.</ns0:text>\n    </ns0:comment>\n    "
          },
          {
            "type": "disruption phenotype",
            "text": "Normal magnetic response, smaller, widely spaced magnetosomes. Near wild-type localization of MamC (PubMed:24816605). Deletion of approximately 80 kb of DNA, including this operon, leads to cells that are non-magnetic, lack internal membrane systems, grow poorly, have reduced mobility and take-up and accumulate iron poorly (PubMed:13129949).",
            "evidence_refs": [],
            "xml": "<ns0:comment xmlns:ns0=\"https://uniprot.org/uniprot\" type=\"disruption phenotype\">\n        <ns0:text evidence=\"2 4\">Normal magnetic response, smaller, widely spaced magnetosomes. Near wild-type localization of MamC (PubMed:24816605). Deletion of approximately 80 kb of DNA, including this operon, leads to cells that are non-magnetic, lack internal membrane systems, grow poorly, have reduced mobility and take-up and accumulate iron poorly (PubMed:13129949).</ns0:text>\n    </ns0:comment>\n    "
          },
          {
            "type": "biotechnology",
            "text": "Chains of magnetosomes (coated with carboxy-methyl-dextran) injected into mouse prostate tumors cause tumor disappearance after ultrasound treatment (6-10 applications of 1 W cm(-2), 1 MHz).",
            "evidence_refs": [],
            "xml": "<ns0:comment xmlns:ns0=\"https://uniprot.org/uniprot\" type=\"biotechnology\">\n        <ns0:text evidence=\"5\">Chains of magnetosomes (coated with carboxy-methyl-dextran) injected into mouse prostate tumors cause tumor disappearance after ultrasound treatment (6-10 applications of 1 W cm(-2), 1 MHz).</ns0:text>\n    </ns0:comment>\n    "
          },
          {
            "type": "miscellaneous",
            "text": "This bacteria makes up to 60 cubo-octahedral magnetosomes of about 45 nm in diameter which contain membrane-bound crystals of magnetite (Fe(3)O(4)).",
            "evidence_refs": [],
            "xml": "<ns0:comment xmlns:ns0=\"https://uniprot.org/uniprot\" type=\"miscellaneous\">\n        <ns0:text evidence=\"8\">This bacteria makes up to 60 cubo-octahedral magnetosomes of about 45 nm in diameter which contain membrane-bound crystals of magnetite (Fe(3)O(4)).</ns0:text>\n    </ns0:comment>\n    "
          },
          {
            "type": "miscellaneous",
            "text": "Expression of just the minimal mamAB gene cluster (MGMSRv2__2365 to MGMSRv2__2381), including this gene, is sufficient to form a minimal magnetosome chain with small magnetite particles.",
            "evidence_refs": [],
            "xml": "<ns0:comment xmlns:ns0=\"https://uniprot.org/uniprot\" type=\"miscellaneous\">\n        <ns0:text evidence=\"3\">Expression of just the minimal mamAB gene cluster (MGMSRv2__2365 to MGMSRv2__2381), including this gene, is sufficient to form a minimal magnetosome chain with small magnetite particles.</ns0:text>\n    </ns0:comment>\n    "
          },
